{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D6KoHKQioTYmJTxbvFKSfV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows\n2\t  \"Version-3 row codec. Pure row construction, graph decoding and canonical\n3\t   cursor-cell numbering; no machine attachment, dependency scanner or transport.\n4\t   An abstract row is {:kind keyword :slots vector}. Structural references\n5\t   contain abstract rows; values use [:lit d], [:row abstract-row], [:cursor-cell id].\n6\t   A task's :cursor-cells row holds alternating source identities and :cursor-cell-body\n7\t   rows. Install children are separate tasks with separate cursor-cell scopes.\n8\t\n9\t   The census is ordered numerically by n (draft §3, \\\"sorted by n\\\"), so\n10\t   :yin.k/cc-10 follows :yin.k/cc-9; its keys must spell cc-N with no leading\n11\t   zero, else :slot-kind.\n12\t\n13\t   Default value markers are plain maps {:yin.k/row abstract-row} and\n14\t   {:yin.k/cursor-cell keyword}. A guest map whose sole key is :yin.k/row or\n15\t   :yin.k/cursor-cell collides with them and is not portable: on encode and decode\n16\t   every literal of that shape is refused :yin.k/non-portable. Explicit\n17\t   markers use the caller value encoder.\"\n18\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n19\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n20\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n21\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t(def profile {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1})\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t(def pending-table\n28\t  {:next [:C]\n29\t   :put [[:ref :stream] :V :D]\n30\t   :ffi [:C :D :D]\n31\t   :ffi-request [:D :V [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\n32\t   :link-request [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D :D]\n33\t   :link-response [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C]\n34\t   :install [:S]})\n35\t\n36\t\n37\t(def row-table\n38\t  \"Slot descriptors, excluding id and kind. :repeat/:pairs are variadic;\n39\t   :refs is an ordered vector