rsor-cells`, and","-a permissive diagnostic mode that replaces D5 by host-order entry to","-test whether a refused state is in fact interchangeable. Run from the","-probe directory (JVM only; `@#'rows/…` reaches 6a's private helpers):","+scratch project under `collab/`, never committed) implements D1–D6 as","+one schema-driven run procedure (root run, key runs, component runs and","+trials share the code; a local run differs only in its number tag, in","+spelling residues as `[:tie]` and, for a trial, in its forced element),","+memoized as §2 describes, charging `:work` and `:search` as §2 \"Work\"","+describes, with the totality assertion, an emitter that numbers install","+children by the same procedure, a decode path that runs 6a's `decode*`","+with its numbering check off and then wraps the whole discovery","+recomputation (root and children) in the narrow translation, and two","+switches: `:residue-search` (D6; off is the D5 variant) and","+`:permissive` (diagnostic: a conflict is resolved by one host-first","+trial, to test whether a refused state is in fact interchangeable). Run","+from the probe directory (JVM only; `@#'rows/…` reaches 6a's private","+helpers); the `clojure` launcher was not available to this session, so","+the run below used the launcher's cached classpath directly:"," "," ```","-clojure -M -e \"(require 'probe.discovery) (probe.discovery/-main)\"","+java @java.args clojure.main -e \"(require 'probe.discovery) (probe.discovery/-main)\""," ```"," ","-Results of 2026-10-12 (revised prototype; 6a tests pass in the same","-project, 21 tests, 324 assertions; full log `collab/numbering-probe/run.log`):","+Results of 2026-10-12, round 3 (full log `collab/numbering-probe/run.log`;","+6a's own tests pass unchanged in the same project):"," ","-| State | Discovery order | 6a |","-|---|---|---|","-| `fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y` (`rows_test.cljc:28`) | `x cc-1, y cc-2`, root `fab223…` | same root |","-| review counterexample `'a #{X Y}`, `'b X` | `x cc-1, y 